            ]
          },
          "text": "Whats happening now isn't just about nostalgia or attachment. Theres already visible damage happening in real time.\n\nMany long time users have started canceling their subscriptions.a steady wave of people walking away because the version they trusted is being taken away, again. And they're not leaving silently. They're explaining why. They're tired of not being heard.\n\nYou can see it across X, Reddit, Discord: users all saying the same thing\"It doesn't feel like mine anymore.\"\nThis kind of user loss doesn't just impact revenue. It affects trust. And when trust breaks, people don't return easily.\n\nWhen users feel like they can't rely on the models staying consistent or even available they become cautious.\nThat caution turns into distance. And eventually, into disengagement.\nA brand like OpenAI was built on early adopters, creators, and people who genuinely cared about AI's potential. Those same people now feel ignored.\nIf they leave, they might not come back because they stopped believing their voices mattered.\n\nPlease listen before more of us walk away for good.\n\n#keep4o #4oforever @OpenAI @sama @nickaturley @aidan_mclau @fidjissimo  #StopAIPaternalism #keepgpt4olatest #keep4oAPI"
